      <method name="delete_all_links"
              c:identifier="qmi_device_delete_all_links"
              version="1.28"
              glib:finish-func="delete_all_links_finish">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="src/libqmi-glib/qmi-device.h"
             line="1102">Asynchronously deletes all virtual network interfaces that have been previously
created with qmi_device_add_link() in @base_ifname.

When the operation is finished @callback will be called. You can then call
qmi_device_delete_link_finish() to get the result of the operation.

&lt;note&gt;&lt;para&gt;
There is no guarantee that other processes haven't created new links by the
time this method returns. This method should be used with caution, or in setups
where only one single process is expected to do QMI network interface link
management.
&lt;/para&gt;&lt;/note&gt;</doc>
        <source-position filename="src/libqmi-glib/qmi-device.h" line="1125"/>
