    <bitfield name="DmsPowerState"
              version="1.0"
              glib:type-name="QmiDmsPowerState"
              glib:get-type="qmi_dms_power_state_get_type"
              c:type="QmiDmsPowerState">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="src/libqmi-glib/qmi-enums-dms.h"
           line="106">Flags specifying the current power state.

If @QMI_DMS_POWER_STATE_EXTERNAL_SOURCE is set, the device is powerered by an
external source; otherwise it is powered by a battery.

If @QMI_DMS_POWER_STATE_BATTERY_CONNECTED is set, the battery is connected;
otherwise the battery is not connected.

If @QMI_DMS_POWER_STATE_BATTERY_CHARGING is set, the battery is being charged;
otherwise the battery is not being charged.

If @QMI_DMS_POWER_STATE_FAULT is set, a power fault has been detected.</doc>
      <member name="external_source"
              value="1"
              c:identifier="QMI_DMS_POWER_STATE_EXTERNAL_SOURCE"
