              c:type="QmiNasNetworkNameDisplayCondition">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="src/libqmi-glib/qmi-enums-nas.h"
           line="1383">Flags used to control display of the PLMN name and Service Provider Name. See
3GPP TS 51.011 descripton of the EFspn SIM file for more details.</doc>
      <member name="registered_plmn_if_known_network"
              value="1"
              c:identifier="QMI_NAS_NETWORK_NAME_DISPLAY_CONDITION_DISPLAY_REGISTERED_PLMN_IF_KNOWN_NETWORK"
              glib:nick="registered-plmn-if-known-network"
              glib:name="QMI_NAS_NETWORK_NAME_DISPLAY_CONDITION_DISPLAY_REGISTERED_PLMN_IF_KNOWN_NETWORK">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="src/libqmi-glib/qmi-enums-nas.h"
             line="1385">if
set, display of the registered PLMN is required when the registered PLMN is either
the HPLMN or a PLMN in the Service Provider PLMN List (see EFspdi). Otherwise
display of the registered PLMN is not required in this case.</doc>
      </member>
      <member name="spn_not_required_if_unknown_network"
              value="2"
              c:identifier="QMI_NAS_NETWORK_NAME_DISPLAY_CONDITION_DISPLAY_SPN_NOT_REQUIRED_IF_UNKNOWN_NETWORK"
              glib:nick="spn-not-required-if-unknown-network"
              glib:name="QMI_NAS_NETWORK_NAME_DISPLAY_CONDITION_DISPLAY_SPN_NOT_REQUIRED_IF_UNKNOWN_NETWORK">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="src/libqmi-glib/qmi-enums-nas.h"
             line="1389">if
set, display of the Service Provider Name is not required when registered PLMN is
neither HPLMN nor a PLMN in the service provider PLMN list (see EFspdi). If not set,
SPN display is required in this case.</doc>
      </member>
